          "id": "104167"
        },
        "body": "I'm not sure entirely what you tested, @NRoach44, and I might also have sent you in the wrong direction. Apologies.\r\n\r\nForgejo Runner clones actions on the host and later copies the actions into the job container when using Docker or Podman. Running `git` as part of a job is only representative of what Forgejo Runner is doing when Forgejo Runner is in host mode. Based on `--labels docker`, Forgejo Runner is not in host mode. That means you'd have to connect to the container that runs `forgejo-runner daemon` and run `git` right there, manually."
      },
